{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1262158-immortal-the-quickening","id":1262158,"title":"Immortal the Quickening","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-22T08:57:36-07:00","id":1262158,"title":"Immortal the Quickening","content":"Well it\u2019s going to be a while before we get a General World of Darkness Vault, so unless I attach this to Vampire or Changeling I probably won\u2019t Vault this project, and I need a to get a new computer because I am not typing on my phone for a whole PDF!<br /> <br /> But I always like the idea of Highlander Style Immortals, but divorced from most of the movies /series. I remember an old Cartoon that was more like what I was thinking where the Highlander took some useful quickenings and what not set in a post apocalyptic future, and then we got that Anime, which was more along what I was thinking.<br /> <br /> But I think it would be fun to treat Immortals more cinematic, and less two normal dudes slapping swords with the occasional spark.<br /> <br /> So my idea first root it in the World of Darkness. So what are Immortals? I\u2019m thinking what if we get them to the 10,000 Immortals and or the Exalted? In fact if I want to avoid copyright issues I would probably call them Exalted in the PDF. So either they are remnants of the Exaltations in Modern time or they are the Chi of the Wan Xian after most were cursed into becoming Wan Gui.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m thinking their splat might be he Aspect of their Quickening. So one for each of the Elements: Flame, Metal, Wood, Earth, Water, Storm/Wind, but also maybe Shadow, Ice, and Light.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re powers revolve around their Aura and Quickening rating. Their expendable energy however works different from most, it would be Pulse, and they get free pulse to use each turn but can spend willpower to channel more.<br /> <br /> Maybe something like:<br /> Quickening\u2014Pulse per turn<br /> 1-1<br /> 2-1<br /> 3-1<br /> 4-2<br /> 5-3<br /> 6-4<br /> 7-5<br /> 8-6<br /> 9-Special<br /> <br /> Each Immortal has an Aspect but also chooses Some Atteibutes they have as Favored.<br /> <br /> Their different Cultivations can channel pulse differently, allowing them to do things like add dice and later successes to certain rolls or remove difficulties.<br /> <br /> They may have a mummy like immortality that can be nullified by removing their noggin.<br /> <br /> They have a normal Experience and Quickening experience. When they slay another Immortal they can roll Quickening of those they killed plus a modifier and take those points in Qexp, which can be spent to raise The Quickening trait.<br /> <br /> They can also learn mortal Sorcery, and some develop Psychic Numina, both of which can be learned by the immortal who slays them.<br /> <br /> Many develop Cultivation\u2019s to bind specific weapons to their Quickening. But I\u2019m thinking of a few that go Full Akuma and are hand to hand experts with full on street fighter moves.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s only a handful on Earth Normally, well I say a handful but that probably means like a Hundred or something, with them often being drawn to each other. After the Red Star Anthelios appeared though a large number of them start Having their second Breaths and are drawn into supernatural conflict. They know the Red Star represents the Gathering as the last of the Immortals are rushing into this Age and they are drawn to become whole. There can be only one, and that one will achieve the Prize.<br /> <br /> But I like the idea both as PCs but also as interesting NPCs to toss into any game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T19:14:00-07:00","id":1262273,"title":"","content":"There was a fan-made version of this floating around the internet 20 years ago. I've no idea if it's still out there somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T19:21:50-07:00","id":1262276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1262158-immortal-the-quickening?p=1262273#post1262273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a fan-made version of this floating around the internet 20 years ago. I've no idea if it's still out there somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I know, a couple actually, I think I can do better after two decades of storytelling tech improvements!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T12:58:35-07:00","id":1262390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1262158-immortal-the-quickening?p=1262273#post1262273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a fan-made version of this floating around the internet 20 years ago. I've no idea if it's still out there somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They also made a 20th version as well!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T13:58:10-07:00","id":1262405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freederp92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1262158-immortal-the-quickening?p=1262390#post1262390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They also made a 20th version as well!</div> </div> </div> </div>What really!? Where?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T14:02:13-07:00","id":1262407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1262158-immortal-the-quickening?p=1262405#post1262405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What really!? Where?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://i.4pcdn.org/tg/1399590846496.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://i.4pcdn.org/tg/1399590846496.pdf</a><br /> <br /> yeah someone updated it, I have yet to run it tho","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T15:16:59-07:00","id":1262421,"title":"","content":"One thing that always disappointed me about the TV series was that, in the original film, when Conner is being trained by Ramirez, the former is shown demonstrating some vague more-than-human abilities, but neither the film nor the TV show ever bothered to develop the idea further. It would've been kind of interesting if one week Duncan had to deal with an immortal who was inhumanly strong or could &quot;cloud men's minds&quot;, and a week or so later runs into an old friend who has an uncanny empathy with animals or is a freakishly skilled artist of some kind. <br /> <br /> As far as splats go, if one were to include them, perhaps based on the classic elements (the chthonic oriented ones of Earth and Water, the olympic oriented ones of Fire and Air, and the mysterious outlier of Aether; the Chinese counterparts being Metal, Water, Fire, Wood, and Earth, respectively). The Kurgan as an example of Earth, perhaps, and Ramirez of Fire. At least that might be one possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-24T13:01:17-07:00","id":1262575,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s what I was talking about with then choosing a Quickening Aspect based off the Elements.<br /> <br /> Curious why do you say Ramirez was Fire?<br /> <br /> But yeah Ramirez hinted at Secret immortal techniques like teaching Conner he didn\u2019t need to breath Air and could get it from the water just as easily, and by modern times they had their swords Arching with lightning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-24T13:44:31-07:00","id":1262580,"title":"","content":"Glanced through the 20th book, seems pretty good for make quick and dirty NPCs. I may borrow some ideas, like the idea Immortals can\u2019t astral Project and Vampires don\u2019t gain nutrients from their blood seems sensible.<br /> <br /> But I\u2019m thinking Different Jedi Powers may come from different Aspects, and from different Attributes. Maybe I should read some more of Forged by Dragons Fire for some ideas.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll draw some inspiration from not just Sword stuff but also things like Matrix and Street Fighter.<br /> <br /> Maybe Eternal Culture would be tied to martial arts Culture around the world, with Traditional Sword duelists most common, other weapons like Axes as eccentric but not rare, and really old school Immortals only using fists. Newer Immortals may use guns and such, with the most pragmatic being like Dante from Devil May Cry using Guns, swords and kicks.<br /> <br /> Maybe I\u2019ll have the powers more like charms then disciplines, so you need a Quickening rating to learn some rather then linear paths. So entry level Cultivation\u2019s, Experienced level Cultivation\u2019s, Elder and then Demigod level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T13:26:08-07:00","id":1262719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1262158-immortal-the-quickening?p=1262575#post1262575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious why do you say Ramirez was Fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly for being outgoing, flamboyant and flashy (compared to the Kurgan, who's dour, grim and relentless). It'd all depend on how such splats would work out, really. <br /> <br /> If you were doing the element thing, you could just as easily go whole hog and use the set up AD&amp;D had back in the day, with the four primary ones (Air, Fire, Water, Earth), the mixed &quot;paraelementals&quot; (Ice, Magma, Ooze and Smoke<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and the energy-influenced quasi-elementals (Lightning, Crystal, Radiance, Steam, Ash, Dust, Salt, and Vacuum). That might be too excessive though. Maybe alternately a Light/Life vs Dark/Death axis and an elemental axis (maybe with a primary and secondary element). Just a thought, anyway. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T14:50:58-07:00","id":1262742,"title":"","content":"Yeah I was contemplating some of those, so I added frost and shadow, I was thinking Rot and Void but was then thinking shadow may cover that.<br /> <br /> I wanted the Quickening to feel unique for each immortal, but I wanted it to be something that would physically manifest, like Conner and lightning but I might have been the Kurgen and storms.<br /> <br /> I was wondering if for instance I would have Dust Be it\u2019s own thing or something that is a type of Earth or wind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T02:26:39-07:00","id":1264397,"title":"","content":"Maybe I should take a not from mummy and give them an easier go at Sorcery, maybe even allow them to learn the beefed up version do Sorcery mummies have.<br /> <br /> And I plan to expand The Mystical Martial Arts known to Mortals in the shadows of the World, perhaps based on Qiao. Immortals could perhaps spend Pulse like Chi and Mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T18:18:35-08:00","id":1265176,"title":"","content":"Random thought that occurred to me: How many of the Changeling the Lost kith powers would work as weird powers an immortal might spontaneously develop for one reason or another?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T21:08:29-08:00","id":1265209,"title":"","content":"Ooh intersting idea! Like 2nd ed?<br /> <br /> Originally I was thinking Mummy the Curse as inspiration with their three tiered Utterance and that other lesser power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T20:13:04-08:00","id":1265433,"title":"","content":"We ran a few Highlander WoD campaigns back in the 90s (during the days of the Highlander TV series) using rules from the wee-beginnings of the internet.<br /> I remember that our games went pretty well and ended epic as well. Of course, like all of WoD, the story usually wraps up with the Final Battle... for The Prize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}